# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plan 00199: rebuilds md-viewer at the M12 commit (non-regular files never block, tracked-files-only
# label test); nothing else changes.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-md-viewer.yml

# Plan 00192 (watermark port): the watermarking play now builds /usr/local/bin/watermark from
# src-go/cmd/watermark (installing the Go toolchain first) in place of the bash script, and
# redeploys the example config whose comments now say the files are read, not sourced. After
# it runs, `watermark --profile <name> photo.jpg` twice (the second exits 3) proves the binary
# (SPEC-wsi-watermark.md section 7, H3). A config file that relied on being sourced (a `$`
# expansion, an unquoted space) is now refused with its file and line.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-image-watermarking.yml

# Plan 00192 (wsi port): the speech-to-text play now builds ~/.local/bin/wsi from src-go/cmd/wsi
# (installing the Go toolchain first) in place of the bash script; the panel extension and the
# sibling helpers are unchanged. After it runs, an Insert, speech, Insert dictation pastes into a
# terminal and an editor, and Escape mid-recording discards it (SPEC-wsi-watermark.md section 7,
# H1 and H2).
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-speech-to-text.yml

# Plans 00161/00201 (team bus security, infrastructure findings): play-agent-bus installs
# Tuwunel 1.9.4 (from 1.9.3) and the re-sandboxed homeserver unit, then RESTARTS EVERY TEAM'S
# HOMESERVER (a few seconds each; members reconnect by themselves). Each now sees only its
# own team's directory and no sibling process; signs in with three wrong passwords allowed,
# then one per five minutes, per account; refuses display-name changes; caps a request at
# 10 MB. Bootstrap deletes the stored admin password (the token stays) and empties any
# agent_bus.status event kept under a key that is no member's. The applied stamps become
# 0640 in a 0750 directory, readable by the desktop user's group only.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
